Description: Remote Desktop sign-in with each account's own password
 Lets Windows' Remote Desktop Connection and other RDP clients open a Patrone
 desktop. Accounts in the remote-desktop group sign in with their own
 username and password, which PAM checks on every connection; nothing keeps a
 copy of them. Each account gets its own desktop, started when it signs in,
 sized to the client's window, and never locked while connected.
 .
 It's off until an administrator runs "patrone-remote-desktop enable".
